emocratic edge"], "rationale": "Ratings, the CNU poll, and market pricing all point to Luria in this even district, offsetting Kiggans's incumbency advantage and the candidates' matched war chests. The margin lands in the mid-single digits for Democrats, short of Likely territory given the thin polling and the district's swing history.", "watch": "A second independent poll in the final weeks or a shift in the national environment could settle it; if Kiggans closes the polling gap, the race reverts to a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jen Kiggans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 2nd District is a rematch between Republican incumbent Jen Kiggans and Democrat Elaine Luria in a district with an even partisan lean. Most race raters now favor Luria: eight of ten call the contest Lean or Likely Democratic, while Cook Political Report and Inside Elections rate it a Tossup. The only recent public poll, from Christopher Newport University in early October, gives Luria a three-point lead among likely voters.\n\nThe candidates are financially matched, each raising about $7.3 million, and outside spending has been limited so far. Prediction markets price Luria's chances near 88 percent, reflecting a favorable national environment for Democrats. Kiggans's incumbency and the district's swing history keep the race competitive, but the combined weight of ratings, polling, and market pricing points to a narrow Democratic edge heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.762, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7557, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7851, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7923, "m